rol Apple music so  Apple is opening up more and they need  to we can just look at history allowing  their services to be used across  different devices has historically been  successful for Apple most people forget  that the original iPod almost flopped  because iTunes was Mac only it was only  after iTunes release on Windows that the  iPod took off and iTunes became the top  digital music store in the world Apple  has also recently bought Shazam  highlighting their interest in  entertainment systems remember the iPod  Touch will there's a possibility that  Apple may be re-releasing it after a  3-year hiatus it's actually a good  entry-level strategy to get new people  into the iOS ecosystem in summary Apple  is facing tough competition in the  smartphone market the biggest revenue  driver it's a market that has pretty  much reached saturation and the end of  its initial life cycle many competitors  provide cheaper alternatives that are  not noticeably inferior to iPhones so  extrapolating what happens in five to  ten years time if Apple stays stagnant  for example what if a company makes a  great foldable phone that's powerful  cheap but actually Pleasant and  convenient to use maybe that's a wild  idea but the point I'm trying to make is  that Apple needs to figure out how to  top the unexpected innovation in the  past half we'll figure out a way to make  a better photo bull phone that works  like magic but what that happen now  Tim Cook does believe that Apple's  foundations and ecosystem are azzolini  enough to withstand the current downturn  and I kind of agree now I have to make  this point very clear Apple has a lot of  cash so they're not going anywhere  anytime soon  but I am noticing a trend and I have  been commenting about Apple losing its  magic for years I did make a video in  2016 talking about this I could see the  trend and now it's starting to come to  life maybe in the future  Apple mostly be a services and software  company who knows  Apple has 